UET Abbottabad - Software Construction (Lab Task 07)

Course: Software Construction (5th Semester Software Engineering)[cite: 1]    
Institution: University of Engineering and Technology, Abbottabad Campus[cite: 1]  

Software Construction Labs
Lab 01 Overview

This repository contains the source code, task implementations, and documentation for Software Construction Labs. The project is structured with a modular package architecture to maintain clean separation of concerns across different assignment tasks.

Project Structure

The project follows a standard package hierarchy located under the com.university.lab namespace:

Task 1: Implements foundational logic and initial problem requirements.

Task 2: Focuses on core component design and structured execution.

Task 3: Handles intermediate data processing and algorithmic workflows.

Task 4: Implements advanced features and system integration.

Main Entry Point

The primary execution point for the entire lab suite is centralized in the runner class:

Class: com.university.lab.lab7.Lab7

Functionality: Coordinates execution flows across all configured task packages.

Task Descriptions

Task 1
This task establishes the basic project configuration and implements the primary initialization routines. It ensures proper data structures and standard input handling are correctly set up.

Task 2
This task introduces object-oriented modularity, focusing on encapsulation and class interactions. It validates core operational logic through structured unit functions.

Task 3
This component implements data filtering, transformation algorithms, and logic handling. It emphasizes clean code principles and efficient execution pathways.

Task 4
This final task integrates the previous modules into a cohesive architecture, demonstrating advanced software construction practices and robust error management.

Conclusion

This lab successfully demonstrates structured Java application development, proper package management, and clean version control workflows using GitHub. All tasks have been verified for modularity, correctness, and clean execution.

Repository Structure & Submission Format
Main File: `com.university.lab.lab7.Lab7.java` serves as the main entry point executing all lab tasks.
Packages:
Task1: Black-Box Reuse via Composition and Interfaces (`PaymentMethod`, `CreditCardPayment`, `JazzCashPayment`, `EcommerceCart`)
Task2: Generic Type Safety containers (`DataBox<T>`)
Task3: Liskov Substitution Principle and Contract Integrity (`Rectangle`, `Square`, `Shape`, `FixedSquare`)
Task4: Reusable Ordering Algorithms (`Student` with `Comparable`, `CgpaComparator`)

